Z||000000||fierospeeder||08-29-2000||12:21 AM||||I was wondering if anyone has bought the tools from JC whitney or eastwood that you can do your own alignment.<P>One is a long bar that fits between the wheels and you can get a tierod measurement.<P>jc whitney also has a roll on type that will tell you tierod plus chamber settings.<P>If so, how accurate are they, i seen the fiero specs and they are plus minus .10.  But im doing this on my tbird. <P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-29-2000||12:46 PM||||I expect such tools are handy if you do any front end work. They should at least get you close enough to not ruin tires in 5 miles. For best results tho you'd likely still want to run a 4 wheel alignment. That's the only way you can check for things like thrust angle problems.||||reg||1
